* The path behind the pond's waterfall to the bamboo-cage lift (openc2e
* Creatures 2 project, our own script; owner's idea, 2026-11-09). Run by
* openc2e after the world loads (Additions folder, after bridges.cos, which
* sets the pond's rooms); safe to repeat. ROOM takes all of a room's data,
* so each room's own values are passed back.
*
* The way is along the pond's bed (owner, 2026-11-10: "not from above, but
* literally just along the pool bed ... going up from the bottom to the left
* into the cave"). The pond (room 19, water, 53 px deep) is shallow enough
* to wade: openc2e lets creatures walk into water no deeper than 55 px, and
* an adult's head stays above it (Room::deepWater). Beyond the pond's west
* end a rock column (room 20, x 4300-4358) stands between the cave and the
* lift shaft (room 21), whose middle stop is at y 840. The rooms:
* - the pond's bed rises at its west end in a ramp (941 to the surface, 888,
*   over 112 px; it was a near-vertical wall) to the foot of the cave's
*   entrance, the hollow behind the waterfall;
* - the rock column (20) is a tunnel behind the rock picture (the world's
*   own foreground cut-out covers it), its floor rising from the pond (888)
*   to level with the shaft's stop (846 at the shaft, 848 20 px on). It
*   was 879 at the shaft, a 39 px step up (steps up to 40 px are walked),
*   but the same step down, out of the shaft, is a fall (over 20 px), and a
*   creature stepping out has its body still over the open shaft, so the
*   fall took it down the shaft, 330 px to the bottom (1175): 23 falls in a
*   5-minute copy of Home (2026-11-18, traced with OPENC2E_WATCH_ROOMS;
*   walking creatures' feet there are at 842-847);
* - the air over the pond (18) has no floor line (an earlier version had a
*   walkway along the cave's back shelf; cleared), and no doorway to the bank
*   or the tunnel; the water opens to the tunnel; the shaft below and the
*   space under the pond stay closed off from the tunnel.
* The waterfall (2 3 1) is drawn in front of creatures (plane 2000, was 1),
* so the path really goes behind it; its mist was already in front.
room 18 4358 810 4630 888 room 18 4 room 18 5 room 18 6 room 18 7 room 18 8 room 18 9 room 18 12 room 18 13 room 18 14 room 18 15 room 18 16 room 18 17 room 18 19
ssfc 18 0
ssfc 19 8 0 53 30 40 70 18 112 0 162 0 222 22 262 45 272 53
room 20 4300 632 4358 941 room 20 4 room 20 5 room 20 6 room 20 7 room 20 8 room 20 9 room 20 12 room 20 13 room 20 14 room 20 15 room 20 16 room 20 17 room 20 19
ssfc 20 3 0 95 20 94 58 53
setv door 0 18 17 0
setv door 0 18 20 0
setv door 0 20 19 255
setv door 0 20 21 255
setv door 0 20 219 0
setv door 0 20 9 0
setv door 0 20 23 0
setv door 0 20 26 0
enum 2 3 1 plne 2000 next
*
* The tunnel's two ends (owner, 2026-11-10). Its entrance: a tall narrow
* hollow in the cave's west wall behind the waterfall, in the space the
* owner outlined, with depth inside: zcvm frame 0 behind creatures, so a
* creature walking west is seen in it until the rock hides it, and frame 1,
* its part over the dark earth, in front of the rock picture (plane 9001;
* original art by art/cavemouth.py); the waterfall's frames are
* used water-only,
* art/cavepath.py, so the creature shows around the water). Its
* exit: the old stone arch west of the lift, its bricked-up back opened into
* a dark passage with a faint glimmer far inside (zcva frame 1, plane -30),
* and the arch's right jamb and the log wall beside it drawn again in front
* of creatures along the opening's edge (zajb, plane 3000, made by
* cavepath.py from the player's own background), so a creature coming out
* walks past the jamb's edge into the arch.
enum 2 3 241 kill targ next
enum 2 3 242 kill targ next
enum 2 3 245 kill targ next
inst new: simp zcvm 1 0 -30 0 setv cls2 2 3 241 setv attr 0 mvto 4338 748 slow
inst new: simp zcvm 1 1 9001 0 setv cls2 2 3 241 setv attr 0 mvto 4338 748 slow
inst new: simp zcva 1 1 -30 0 setv cls2 2 3 242 setv attr 0 mvto 4040 712 slow
inst new: simp zajb 1 0 3000 0 setv cls2 2 3 245 setv attr 0 mvto 4078 700 slow
*
* The hidden doorway: rooms cannot run a tunnel behind the lift shaft (the
* lift needs the shaft's rooms), so a watcher (2 1 150, invisible) carries a
* creature that walks west through the tunnel, while hidden behind the rock
* at its west end (centre x 4300-4332, feet at the tunnel's floor, 836-896,
* facing left; it looked for feet at 866 or lower until 2026-11-22, as the
* floor was before it was raised to the shaft's stop, and took only some of
* them), to the arch: standing on the arch's floor (840) with its right
* side at x 4180, hidden behind the jamb drawn in front (a creature wider
* than the jamb's 64 px already shows inside the opening), still walking
* west, out past the jamb's edge. Going east, a creature crosses the lift's shaft into the
* rock as before: a script can't tell one bound for the cave from one bound
* for the lift.
enum 2 1 150 kill targ next
inst new: simp blnk 1 0 0 0 setv cls2 2 1 150 setv attr 16 mvto 4320 640 tick 1 slow
scrp 2 1 150 9
* inst: in one tick (without it two of every three ticks were skipped while
* the last look was still running; measured 2026-11-12)
  inst
  enum 4 0 0
    doif movs eq 0
      setv var0 posl addv var0 posr divv var0 2
      doif var0 ge 4300
        doif var0 le 4332
          doif posb ge 836
            doif posb le 896
              doif dirn eq 3
                setv var1 4180 subv var1 posr addv var1 posl
                setv var2 839 subv var2 posb addv var2 post
                mvto var1 var2
              endi
            endi
          endi
        endi
      endi
    endi
  next
endm
*
* The falls drawn see-through while a creature is behind them (owner,
* 2026-11-10: checkered with transparent pixels, like the hand). The falls
* are in front of creatures (plane 2000); a watcher (2 1 151, invisible,
* every 2 ticks) stipples them (STPL, openc2e's: every other pixel left out
* in a checkerboard) while any creature overlaps the water (x 4374-4432,
* y 734-887; the water-only falls' pixels), and draws them whole otherwise.
* (Its OV00 is 1 while they are stippled.)
enum 2 1 151 kill targ next
inst new: simp blnk 1 0 0 0 setv cls2 2 1 151 setv attr 16 mvto 4320 640 tick 2 slow
scrp 2 1 151 9
  inst
  setv var0 0
  enum 4 0 0
    doif posr gt 4376
      doif posl lt 4430
        doif posb gt 736
          doif post lt 885
            setv var0 1
          endi
        endi
      endi
    endi
  next
  setv ov00 var0
  enum 2 3 1 stpl var0 0 next
endm
*
* The pond's fish kept in the water (owner, 2026-11-10: fish seemed to go
* above the water and get stuck). The pond (room 19) is open at its sides,
* to the bank (room 17) and to the hidden tunnel (room 20), so creatures can
* wade in and out; a doorway can't let creatures through and stop fish, so
* the pond's fish (2 20 9, which flop about out of water and die after
* about 30 s) swam out at its edges and were stranded. A watcher (2 1 152,
* invisible, every 5 ticks) puts any fish found out of water around the
* pond (x 4300-4900, y 780-1000) back into it, near the edge it left by.
enum 2 1 152 kill targ next
inst new: simp blnk 1 0 0 0 setv cls2 2 1 152 setv attr 16 mvto 4320 640 tick 5 slow
scrp 2 1 152 9
  inst
  enum 2 20 0
    doif spcs eq 9
      doif rtyp ne 2
        doif posx gt 4300
          doif posx lt 4900
            doif posy gt 780
              doif posy lt 1000
                setv var0 4590
                doif posx lt 4495 setv var0 4385 endi
                setv velx 0 setv vely 0
                mvto var0 905
              endi
            endi
          endi
        endi
      endi
    endi
  next
endm

* The bamboo-cage lift (3 2 2, cabin x 4172-4275) stands in front of the
* path: the tunnel from the waterfall crosses its shaft at the middle stop
* (y 840) and goes on west behind the tower. The lift was at plane 0, behind
* creatures (1500), so a creature walking through while the lift waited at
* that stop showed over the cage, as if riding it, though it was hidden by
* the tower's stone when the lift was elsewhere (owner, 2026-11-13). At
* plane 1600 the cage is in front of creatures walking past; its riders,
* drawn at the lift's plane + 1, still show inside it, and the tower's stone
* pillars (8999) still cover both.
enum 3 2 2 doif posx gt 4100 and posx lt 4300 plne 1600 endi next
